        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "docs(repair): explain automatic issue PR flow",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds a maintainer-facing guide that explains when ClawSweeper can turn an issue into its own repair PR, and when it only reviews, reports on, or queues that issue.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe repository had the individual workflow and repair-operation documents, but no single guide explaining why two superficially similar issues can receive different automatic issue-to-PR treatment.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Adds `docs/repair/automatic-issue-prs.md`, covering scheduled review, automatic intake, explicit maintainer commands, autonomous execution, contributor-PR adoption, credentials, limits, and duplicate guards.\n- Links the guide from the repair documentation index.\n- Adds it to the generated documentation-site Repair navigation.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `node scripts/build-docs-site.mjs`\n- `node --test test/docs-site-theme.test.ts`\n- Local relative-link check for `docs/repair/automatic-issue-prs.md`\n- `git diff --check`\n\n## Proof\n\nThe docs-site build generated 36 pages successfully, the theme test passed, and the changed document's local links resolve.\n\n### Codex review closeout\n\nRan focused uncommitted-diff reviews throughout drafting. Accepted findings tightened distinctions between scheduled and command-driven paths, the viable-route eligibility rule, audit deduplication, comment-router artifacts, post-intake pause handling, and the separate planning/status/executor token scopes. Focused proof was rerun after each accepted fix.\n\nFinal clean reviews:\n\n- `codex review --uncommitted` — no actionable findings.\n- `codex review --base origin/main` — no actionable findings; documentation and navigation were consistent with the implemented flow and the generated docs site built successfully.\n\n## Risks and rollout\n\nThis changes documentation and docs-site navigation only. The guide deliberately links to the corresponding source and workflow documents so operational gates remain verifiable as the implementation evolves.\n\nUser-facing note: maintainers now have one place to explain why an issue was reviewed, queued, or turned into a ClawSweeper repair PR.\n\n## Links\n\n- New guide: `docs/repair/automatic-issue-prs.md`\n- Existing repair guide: `docs/repair/README.md`\n- Operations runbook: `docs/operations/repair-operations.md`\n",
